Match the two lines of a sunken separator

The vertical branch of the tool bar separator draws its first line with
the gap macro. It draws its second line with the literals six and
twelve. The macro gives five while the option for faded lines holds
true, and that is the shipped value. The two lines then hold different
end points, and the second line loses one row at each end. The
horizontal branch of the same paint takes the macro for both lines.

The second line now takes the gap from the macro as well. The two lines
share their end points under every value of the faded lines option. A
configuration with no faded lines keeps the paint of before.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 18 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp
